  {
   "tab": "Gas pipelines",
   "row": 4584,
   "column": "DataCenterNotes",
   "cell": "EE4584",
   "value": "A Pipeline and Gas Journal article from July 2025, citing East Daley Analytics, says the project targets demand from data centers, petrochemical plants and power generators. It says that if the line were fully dedicated to data center use it could support 125 to 150 megawatts of load. The company notice mentions behind the meter uses tied to artificial intelligence. No specific data center is named.",
